# Patterns the organisation-string gate refuses (scripts/org-gate.mjs; docs/conventions.md §13).
# Copy this file to .org-gate.local, fill in the real strings, and NEVER commit the copy: it names the private origin.
# One JavaScript regular expression per line, matched case-insensitively; `#` starts a comment.
#
# The six classes, with placeholders. Keep a line per spelling (with and without separators, abbreviations, old names).

# 1. product and company names
\byourproduct\b
\byour[-_ ]?company\b

# 2. the company's domains and every host under them
(^|[^a-z0-9.-])yourcompany\.(com|io|ai|dev)\b
\b[a-z0-9-]+\.internal\.yourcompany\.com\b

# 3. mail addresses and address ranges on those domains
qa\+[a-z0-9-]+@yourcompany\.com
@yourcompany\.com\b

# 4. people's and teams' names, cloud profile or account ids
\bfirstname lastname\b
\bteam-codename\b
\bacct-[0-9]{6,}\b

# 5. internal document and case-list ids, ticket keys, runbook names
\bDOC-[0-9]{3,}\b
\b[A-Z]{2,5}-[0-9]{2,5}\b
\brunbook-codename\b

# 6. the private framework's own cookie names, header names and environment-variable prefix
\byour_session_cookie\b
\bX-Your-Runner-Key\b
\bYOURPREFIX_[A-Z]
